; A type choice containing `bool` — pins the CLOSURE of the former "type annotations needed"
; (E0282) finding. `bool / tstr` and `uint / bool` once generated non-compiling Rust because the
; pre-cbor_event-3.x serialize/deserialize fns carried reader/writer generics that left the
; bool-arm's inferred type unconstrained; the 3.x de-generification (concrete `Serializer`/
; `Deserializer`) removed that hazard, so both orderings now generate and round-trip under every
; profile (default / preserve / json). Both bool-first (`bool / tstr`) and bool-last
; (`uint / bool`) orderings are exercised because the annotation hazard was position-sensitive.
; The canonical `type.choice` fixture stays `type_choice.cddl` (steered off `bool` to isolate the
; `/` construct itself, per the type_and_ranges.toml example note); this file isolates the
; bool-in-choice hazard specifically, so a regression re-introducing the generics fails the corpus
; compile gate here rather than going unpinned.
bool_or_text = bool / tstr
uint_or_bool = uint / bool
